{"name":"Mad About You","hex":"#a9324b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Madurese."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Insane; crazy; mentally deranged.","Angry; annoyed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mad"},{"term":"about","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["In a circle around; all round; on every side of; on the outside of; around. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Over or upon different parts of; through or over in various directions; here and there in; to and fro in; throughout."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On all sides, or in every or any direction from a point; around.","Here and there; around; in one place and another; up and down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/about"},{"term":"you","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["The people spoken, or written to, as an object. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","(To) yourselves, (to) yourself."]},{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["The individual or group spoken or written to.","Used before epithets, describing the person being addressed, for emphasis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/you"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mad About You","blocks":[{"text":"Mad About You is an American television sitcom starring Paul Reiser and Helen Hunt as a married couple in New York City as they navigate life together. In later seasons, the couple has a daughter."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mad_About_You","wikidata":"Q752365"},{"title":"Mad About You (Belinda Carlisle song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Mad About You\" is a song by American singer Belinda Carlisle. It was written by Paula Jean Brown, James Whelan and Mitchel Young Evans, and produced by Michael Lloyd for Carlisle's debut solo album, Belinda. The song was released in 1986 as Carlisle's debut solo single after leaving the Go-Go's. The song peaked at number three on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 chart and at number one on Canada's RPM 100 Singles chart. The song was later included in the jukebox musical Head over Heels that used the Go-Go's music in addition to two of Carlisle's solo tracks. The musical debuted on Broadway in 2018."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Belindacarlisle_Mad_About_You.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mad_About_You_(Belinda_Carlisle_song)","wikidata":"Q1321864"},{"title":"You","blocks":[{"text":"In Modern English, the word \"you\" is the second-person pronoun. It is grammatically plural, and was historically used only for the dative case, but in most modern dialects is used for all cases and numbers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You","wikidata":"Q1165897"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"mad":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/En-us-mad.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b6/En-us-mad.ogg/En-us-mad.ogg.mp3"}],"about":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-about.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-about.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-about.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-about.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-about.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"opus\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/En-us-about_%28improved%29.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg",